{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Software Engineering: the Interface "}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about software interface elements:"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understands systems theories, business processes and basic concepts on IT.  Create a map of processes that allows identifying areas in an information system, using IT tools to generate reports based on the company's needs."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level. Exchanges simple information on IT concepts, systems theory, and diagrams of processes."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Present Tense - Affirmative Form"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\"> simple present</span> tense to talk about general actions, habits and processes.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "In general, you use the <span class=\"strong\">simple present in affirmative </span> to make statements for repetitive  or actions,  facts, habits and things that are always or generally true."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember that the structure that we follow for the affirmative form is:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\">Subject + <span class=\"strong\">verb (add s if it is third person) </span>+ complement.<br><br></div>  For Example: <br><span class=\"italic\">Interfaces <span class=\"strong\">work</span> as a perfect medium between users.<br />The hardware interface <span class=\"strong\">comprehends</span> a lot of connections.</div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div align=\u201djustify\u201d>It is important to remember that when we conjugate the verbs in present, they can change depending on the type of subject the sentence has. Check the following chart:</div> <br> <br> <span class=\"strong\"> <div class=\"center_text\">HOW TO ADD THE -S TO THIRD PERSON / SPELLING RULE</span>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"For verbs that end in <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> -O, -CH, -SH, -SS, -X, or -Z </span> we add <span class=\\\"strong\\\">ES</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<li>fix \u2013 fix<span class=\\\"strong\\\">es</span></li><br /><li>catch \u2013 catch<span class=\\\"strong\\\">es</span></li>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"For verbs that end in a <span class=\\\"strong\\\">consonant + Y</span> , we remove the <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Y </span>and add <span class=\\\"strong\\\">-IES.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<li> study \u2013 stud<span class=\\\"strong\\\">ies</span></li><br /><li> carry \u2013 carr<span class=\\\"strong\\\">ies</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"For verbs that end in a  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">vowel + Y</span>, we just add<span class=\\\"strong\\\">-S.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<li> enjoy \u2013 enjoy<span class=\\\"strong\\\">s</span></li><br /><li> say \u2013 say<span class=\\\"strong\\\">s</span></li>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "A very important part of software engineering is the interface. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Now, that interface takes place under different circumstances. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "All in all, the software interface is basically a language and message format as the system uses commands and codes to communicate and transfer data from point A to point B."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Interface"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use an <span class=\"strong\">interface </span> to exchange information among different elements or components of a computer system. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "An interface does not only happen between the components of a computer, but it happens when there is an interaction between a human and a machine, too. For example, devices like touchscreens send and receive data through an interface; plus, devices such as the mouse or microphone provide an interface to send data to a system"}, {"type": "text", "content": "We can also define interface as a supporting arrangement to the connection between devices. However, there are two different types of interface, the hardware interface and the software interface. Check the following chart to learn about them: "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">HARDWARE INTERFACE</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">SOFTWARE INTERFACE</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\u201djustify\u201d>Transfers data from an external device to the computer's internal elements through <span class=\\\"strong\\\">signaling </span>, a sequence of mechanical, electrical and logical signals.</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\u201djustify\u201d>Transfers information among programs and applications through <span class=\\\"strong\\\">streams </span>, sequences of data that are available one at a time.   Software can interface with hardware, too.</div>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are some important terms that we have to learn about hardware and software interface. Check the table below:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">HARDWARE INTERFACE</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">SOFTWARE INTERFACE</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Parallel</span>: Several connections taking parts of data at the same time from one side to another. <br>   <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Serial</span>: Sends data one bit at a time. <br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Constant</span>: Identifiers that get an associated value and that you cannot change. <br>  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Data Types</span>: Classification according to types of data, the value, the path of operation for  such data, and the way the system records the value. <br>  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Subroutine</span>: A sequence of program instructions that perform a specific task. <br>  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Exception handling</span>: The process of facing the emergence of an exception during computation. <br>  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Type of signature</span>: Defines the inputs and outputs for a function, subroutine or method. \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "device "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an electronic element"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When we talk about that, we refer to the different types of connections or interactions between two different systems or devices. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob03aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "printer "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a machine we use for printing a document or file"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: For example, a printer receives printing information from a computer through an interface. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob03aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "plug "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the end of a cable or wire"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Furthermore, this type of interface contemplates connectors, ports and plugs that link devices, such as the mouse or keyboard, to a computer. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob03aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "link "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to connect two different elements "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I want to do a contextualization and give brief information about the interface, a complex concept. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob03aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "enable "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to permit, to make possible "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Now, we can say that this type of interface basically enables the communication of different programs with each other or with the operating system."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob03aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about software and hardware interface."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Divide a chart in two parts and in one side, write all the hardware you find and in the other, write all the software you find."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write how the interfaces for them are."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your chart with the class and deci